Review the revised complete RFC-257 WS-E DESIGN (v2), not implementation. Repo /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go. Candidate TREE cec59465947ae903c45373d8935f91aab96628e0; design rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-e-design.md SHA256 a1649fa04ee44a68b45fc3133b7749fc9abb11ee18a519ea4acb97a62fb30baf. Previous: v1 TREE cc94face9f554e277346f6061becf84c658abc3b (three NAKs: rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-e-design-review-v1/{graefe,torvalds,storage}.txt). Umbrella: rfcs/257-java-4.14.2.0-upgrade.md section "WS-E" (two corrections by the oracle are marked there); audits build-docs W4-W6, cascades W1-W2/W11, relational W1-W3/W10. WS-E1 (FROM-less SELECT) is already accepted and out of scope.
The design's target contracts rest on a live-JVM oracle IN THE TREE: conformance/ws_e_probe_conformance_test.go, three Describes in //conformance:rfc257_oracle_test: "WS-E target oracle" (74 pinned, unchanged), "WS-E target oracle v2" (37 pinned: LIKE error timing, B64/decorated literals, EXPLAIN+SNAPSHOT, variadic admission, eager evaluation, result nullability from result-set metadata, several/named/typed parameters) and "WS-E target oracle v2 extended" (12 pinned: ORDER BY a constant, SNAPSHOT as a CONNECTION option, prepared DML into an INTEGER column, mixed/repeated named parameters, IN ? with an array parameter, UUID parameter). Supporting test-harness changes: result sets carry JDBC nullability (conformance/sql_plan_steps.java resultSetToJson; plandiff.RowSet.Nullability, filled by both runners), a new Java step runPreparedExtended, and plandiff.PreparedDMLRunner. Evidence: rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-e-oracle/evidence-run.txt and evidence-mutations.txt (v2 rounds appended; each round run twice with identical Java lines; a mutated pin reddens). Full run logs: /var/tmp/fdb-upgrade-recovery/ws-e2-4.log and ws-e3-2.log (Read tool). No WS-E production code exists yet. The tree also carries other RFC-257 work (WS-D design v9 and its oracle, WS-J oracle and trie fix, heartbeat predicate) that has its own gates.
Tree objects: run `git show TREE:path` and `git diff OLD NEW` from the repo root (the read-only policy admits commands that START with the git subcommand, or `git -C /home/birdy/projects/fdb-go ...`; avoid shell variables and `cd ... &&` chains). Java tag 4.14.2.0 at fdacd162a9c8acfadc49082b89185c823ab8ae4a in fdb-record-layer/ (read fdb-record-layer/.git/HEAD if rev-parse is denied).
Read ALL three v1 verdicts, the FULL v2 design and its diff from v1, the oracle spec and evidence, and check every claim against actual Java and current Go. v2's answers to v1: bound NULL is untyped (no api.NullOf); the cache key uses the target's fold (literal-named tokens only, uid through the analyzer's normalization, statement options out of the text, PLAN RIGHT DEEP in a planner-configuration component); LIKE errors raised per evaluated row (measured) and the matcher over runes; decorated literals rejected with the target's messages; variadic admission per the target's operator map (BYTES/UUID/ENUM rejected, DATE/TIMESTAMP kept as a declared extension), INCOMPATIBLE_TYPE 22000, the blanket ScalarFunctionValue nullability override removed with its dependents, the COALESCE fold narrowed to what EvaluateConstantCoalesceRule folds; the nullable-array extension bounded by CONSUMER (comparison operands); typed binding with named/mixed/array/UUID parameters, value copying, bit-exact key rendering, an invalid-UTF-8 refusal, textual ordinals with the target's visitor-order ordinal defect measured and declared, and the target's strict LONG-into-INTEGER assignment; snapshot at connection and statement scope, the target's read scope (index fetch serializable), per-page application in Go's auto-commit paging, a bool not the zero-value enum, a typed DML backstop, and the continuation/COPY arms handed to WS-G/WS-K. Challenge sufficiency, the declared divergences (each necessary?), whether the consumer-based nullable-array rule is structural, the cache key's injectivity and scope, the binding/lifetime contract, and test sufficiency (mutation-checkable, cold and warm cache, real FDB conflict behaviour). Distinguish measured target facts from source hypotheses.
Preserved boundaries: approved Go read/raw nullable-array, scalar and sorting extensions; the Go-only IN-subquery read extension; LIMIT (Go extension); one Cascades pipeline; C++ 7.3.77; no wire change unless the design proves Java writes it.
Actual reviewer gate run via `claude -p` (model opus, effort xhigh) under a read-only tool policy (Read/Grep/Glob plus read-only git/grep/sed Bash; no Edit/Write). The owner authorized this substitution for the exhausted Codex account. No tests/probes/mutations/edits/staging/commits/push/CI/PR/publication/operational changes. Return ACK or NAK, the exact tree and design hash, and actionable findings with source line references ordered by severity. Incomplete review is not ACK. Under 900 words unless needed.

Apply the independent storage/wire correctness review lens: what bound values can reach stored records and index keys (UTF-8, widths, assignment lattice), snapshot read scope and read-conflict/commit semantics on real FDB, paging transactions, plan-cache sharing across isolation levels, value lifetime in cached plans, and that no persisted bytes change.
